// The multi-bit fill's Rule G test (row 506; Ruminations\row-460-rules-and-tests-2026-11-18.md, B1 and section 4 test 1;
// the model check's m1, m2, m3 and m6): A FILL WHOSE COMPARE-AND-SWAP SUCCEEDS ON THE PAGE'S NEXT LIFE MUST GIVE EVERY
// TAKEN BIT BACK IN ONE FETCH_OR, PASSING THE LIFE IT TOOK THEM FROM, AND MUST WRITE NO CELL. Every step is driven.
//
// A worker thread (the filler; cnmalloc_workerBegin, CNMALLOC cache=16, so its fills grow 2, 4, 8 and stay at 8) fills from
// the 1024-byte class (64 cells, one word of bits a page; slots=1). Its fill is parked by the shim's first park point, after
// it loaded the word and before its compare-and-swap. The main thread then makes the page wholly free, retires it (a forced
// collect, twice), takes it back from the pool as a 512-byte page and stamps that life's cells (first and last word), and
// arranges that the word reads as the filler loaded it. The filler is released: its swap succeeds on the new life, and it is
// parked again between its swap and its g2 load (LF_HOOK_TAKE), where the word must show the whole take gone in one swap;
// then once more right after the undo's fetch_or, where the word must show every taken bit back. Afterwards no stamp may be
// overwritten (MB-W: no link written with the old class's size), every bit is restored, and the multi-bit undo count rose
// by one.
// Two kinds of round:
//   partial: the page was wholly free when the filler loaded the word, so it takes 8 of 64; the undo cannot leave the word
//     wholly free on an attached page, so the slow path is not entered.
//   whole word (m6's shape, the model's mbs4): the filler loaded a word with exactly 8 free bits and takes all of them, so
//     the new life's word is 0 after its swap. While it is parked between the swap and g2, the main thread allocates a
//     512-byte cell, finds the page full and detaches it (UNLISTED). The undo then finds old == 0 on a page that is not in a
//     slot and takes "after a free", which must take the 512 class's lock (the life the bits came from) and list the page.
//     An undo that passed g1 would take the 1024 class's lock, fail the generation test and leave the page UNLISTED with
//     free bits: lost, with no crash. So the round ends by checking that the page is LISTED with every bit restored.
// Same-class rounds (row 701; they catch mutant a2, whose Rule G compares the class half of genclass only): the whole-word
//   shape, but the retired page comes back as the SAME 1024 class with a new generation (CNMULTI_SAME rounds, default 10).
//   The whole genclass differs, so the swap must be undone: the count rises by one, every bit is restored, no stamp is hit.
//   Under a2 the filler keeps 8 cells of the page's earlier life, so the word is not restored and the count does not rise.
// Single-cell rounds (row 532; they catch mutant a2s, the same class-half compare in lf_alloc's Rule G): a second thread, the
//   taker, is NOT a worker, so its malloc goes to lf_alloc. It loads a word with only its highest cell free and is parked before
//   its swap; the page retires and comes back as the SAME 1024 class with a new generation, its word made to read as the taker
//   loaded it. Released, the taker's swap takes the one bit and it is parked between the swap and g2 (LF_HOOK_TAKE, which
//   lf_alloc shares with lf_fill), where the word must read 0; the main thread's allocation then detaches the full page. Then
//   right after the undo's fetch_or. The whole-genclass compare must undo the take: Rule G's undo count (lfTotal 9) rises by
//   one and the multi-bit count (10) does not, the bit is restored, no stamp is hit, the page ends LISTED, and the taker's
//   cell is not the one it gave back. Under a2s the taker keeps the cell: it never reaches the undo's park point, the word
//   stays 0, the count does not rise and the page stays UNLISTED (CNMULTI_SINGLE rounds, default 10).
// Three control rounds (the page does not change) must take 8 cells of one page normally, with no undo. At the end, with
// every cell freed and the filler's cache emptied, allocations equal frees.
//
// Needs cnd.lib (-DCN_HOOKS -DCN_DEBUG) and CNMALLOC=design=lockfree,giveback=now,slots=1,stats,cache=16:
//   $env:_LINK_ = '"<dir>\cnd.lib"'; $env:CNMALLOC = 'design=lockfree,giveback=now,slots=1,stats,cache=16'   (delete build\ first),
//   then 'congo test lfmulti'. CNMULTI_ROUNDS=<n> partial rounds (default 20), CNMULTI_WHOLE=<n> whole-word rounds (default 10),
//   CNMULTI_SAME=<n> same-class rounds (default 10), CNMULTI_SINGLE=<n> single-cell rounds (default 10).
// Under a plain 'congo test' nothing is linked and the test passes without testing. tests/mutants.ps1 runs it against a2m, a2s,
// m1, m2, m3 and m6, each of which must fail it.

mod lfmulti;

import testing use *;
import thread;
import libc;

extern {
  fn @c(system) Sleep(ms: u32);
  fn @c(system) SwitchToThread() i32;
  fn @c(system) QueryPerformanceCounter(t: *i64) i32;
  fn @c(system) QueryPerformanceFrequency(f: *i64) i32;
  fn @c(system) GetStdHandle(n: u32) usize;
  fn @c(system) WriteFile(h: usize, buf: *u8, n: u32, written: *u32, ov: usize) i32;
  fn @c(system) CreateFileA(name: *u8, access: u32, share: u32, sec: usize, disp: u32, flags: u32, tmpl: usize) usize;
  fn @c(system) CloseHandle(h: usize) i32;
  fn @c(system) ExitProcess(code: u32);
  fn @c(system) GetModuleHandleA(name: *u8) usize;
  fn @c(system) GetProcAddress(module: usize, name: *u8) usize;
  fn @c("_msize") msize(p: *u8) usize;
  fn @c("strlen") strlen(s: cstr) usize;
  fn @c("strncpy") copyLit(d: *u8, s: cstr, n: usize) *u8;
}

alias SetHooks = &fn @c (pre: usize, detach: usize, retire: usize, claim: usize, afterOr: usize, after: usize);
alias SetMulti = &fn @c (take: usize, group: usize);
alias Collect = &fn @c (force: i32) u64;
alias DesignFn = &fn @c () i32;
alias Total = &fn @c (which: i32) i64;
alias Peek = &fn @c (p: usize, which: i32) u64;
alias Begin = &fn @c ();

// words of the control block
const cCmd = 0usize;        // 1: the filler takes 8 cells (cOut..); 2: it ends its worker cache and stops
const cDone = 1usize;
const cBegin = 2usize;      // cnmalloc_workerBegin and cnmalloc_workerEnd
const cEnd = 3usize;
const cArmPre = 4usize;     // the filler's next visit to a park point parks there
const cParkedPre = 5usize;
const cRelPre = 6usize;
const cArmTake = 7usize;
const cParkedTake = 8usize;
const cRelTake = 9usize;
const cArmOr = 10usize;
const cParkedOr = 11usize;
const cRelOr = 12usize;
const cSeenOld = 13usize;   // the word the filler loaded (first park point)
const cSeenWant = 14usize;  // the bits it took (LF_HOOK_TAKE)
const cN = 15usize;         // how many cells command 1 takes
const cOut = 16usize;       // the filler's cells (8 a round)
const cWords = 32usize;

const ones = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFu64;

var @threadlocal fctl: usize = 0usize;

fn at(p: *u8, i: usize) *u8 { ((p as usize) + i) as *u8 }
fn word(base: usize, i: usize) *usize { (base + i * 8usize) as *usize }
fn ld(base: usize, i: usize) usize { mem.atomicLoad[usize](word(base, i), MemOrder.SeqCst) }
fn st(base: usize, i: usize, v: usize) { mem.atomicStore[usize](word(base, i), v, MemOrder.SeqCst); }

fn spinUntil(c: usize, i: usize) {
  while ld(c, i) == 0usize { SwitchToThread(); }
}

fn park(c: usize, arm: usize, seen: usize, v: usize) {
  if c != 0usize && ld(c, arm) == 1usize {
    st(c, arm, 0usize);
    if seen != 0usize { st(c, seen, v); }
    st(c, arm + 1usize, 1usize);
    spinUntil(c, arm + 2usize);
  }
}

// the shim's park points, on the filler only: before a fill's swap; between a fill's swap and its g2 load; after a fetch_or
fn @c hookPre(cl: usize, old: u64) { park(fctl, cArmPre, cSeenOld, usize.from(old)); }
fn @c hookTake(cl: usize, want: u64) { park(fctl, cArmTake, cSeenWant, usize.from(want)); }
fn @c hookOr(cl: usize) { park(fctl, cArmOr, 0usize, 0usize); }

// the filler (a worker) and the taker (row 532: the same loop on its own control block, with cBegin and cEnd 0, so it stays a
// non-worker and its malloc goes to lf_alloc)
fn filler(arg: usize) u64 {
  let c = arg;
  fctl = c;
  if ld(c, cBegin) != 0usize { (ld(c, cBegin) as *u8 as Begin)(); }
  while true {
    let cmd = ld(c, cCmd);
    if cmd == 1usize {
      st(c, cCmd, 0usize);
      var i = 0usize;
      while i < ld(c, cN) { st(c, cOut + i, libc.malloc(1024usize) as usize); i = i + 1usize; }
      st(c, cDone, 1usize);
    } else if cmd == 2usize {
      if ld(c, cEnd) != 0usize { (ld(c, cEnd) as *u8 as Begin)(); }
      st(c, cDone, 1usize);
      break;
    } else {
      SwitchToThread();
    }
  }
  0u64
}

const cStop = 31usize;      // set by main when the test is over; the watchdog ends on it

// a mutant that corrupts a free list can hang the allocator itself (row 701: a2); the watchdog turns that into a failure
fn watchdog(c: usize) u64 {
  var t = 0usize;
  while t < 240usize {
    if ld(c, cStop) == 1usize { return 0u64; }
    Sleep(500u32);
    t = t + 1usize;
  }
  errLine("lfmulti: WATCHDOG: no end after seconds ", 120usize, "; stuck cell chain? round state ", 0usize, " ", 0usize);
  ExitProcess(3u32);
  0u64
}

// the monotonic clock (QueryPerformanceCounter), in milliseconds
fn nowMs() i64 {
  var f = 0i64;
  var t = 0i64;
  QueryPerformanceFrequency(&mut f);
  QueryPerformanceCounter(&mut t);
  (t / f) * 1000i64 + ((t % f) * 1000i64) / f
}

// (row 532) until word i is `want`, or about 5 s of the monotonic clock have passed (false: the caller's check fails).
// Counting Sleep(1)s was ~78 s at Windows' 15.6 ms tick, so a hung mutant was caught only by the 120 s watchdog.
fn waitFor(c: usize, i: usize, want: usize) bool {
  let end = nowMs() + 5000i64;
  while ld(c, i) != want && nowMs() < end { Sleep(1u32); }
  ld(c, i) == want
}

// (row 532) until word i or word j is set: a round that can tell "no park point reached" from the thread finishing, without
// waitFor's full time-out (5000 Sleep(1)s, about 78 s at Windows' default 15.6 ms timer)
fn waitEither(c: usize, i: usize, j: usize) {
  let end = nowMs() + 5000i64;
  while ld(c, i) == 0usize && ld(c, j) == 0usize && nowMs() < end { Sleep(1u32); }
}

fn cleanup(coll: Collect) { coll(1i32); coll(1i32); }

fn stamp(p: usize, size: usize, v: usize) {
  *word(p, 0usize) = size;
  *word(p, size / 8usize - 1usize) = v;
}

fn stampOk(p: usize, size: usize, v: usize) bool {
  *word(p, 0usize) == size && *word(p, size / 8usize - 1usize) == v
}

// the filler takes 8 cells (each round's fill); false when it did not finish
fn fill8(c: usize) bool {
  st(c, cDone, 0usize);
  st(c, cCmd, 1usize);
  waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize)
}

// the filler's 8 cells: all of the 1024 class, distinct, on one page; then freed by the main thread (not a worker)
fn checkFree8(c: usize) usize {
  var errs = 0usize;
  let p0 = ld(c, cOut);
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < 8usize {
    let p = ld(c, cOut + i);
    if p == 0usize || msize(p as *u8) != 1024usize || p >> 16usize != p0 >> 16usize { errs = errs + 1usize; }
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < i { if ld(c, cOut + k) == p { errs = errs + 1usize; } k = k + 1usize; }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  i = 0usize;
  while i < 8usize { let p = ld(c, cOut + i); if p != 0usize { libc.free(p as *u8); } i = i + 1usize; }
  errs
}

fn release(c: usize, rel: usize) { st(c, rel, 1usize); }

fn resetParks(c: usize) {
  var i = cArmPre;
  while i <= cRelOr { st(c, i, 0usize); i = i + 1usize; }
}

// counts kept by the rounds
const kErr = 0usize;        // anything wrong at all (each check that failed)
const kTake = 1usize;       // rounds whose swap took the expected bits in one compare-and-swap
const kUndo = 2usize;       // rounds whose undo restored every taken bit in its one fetch_or
const kStamp = 3usize;      // stamps overwritten
const kRestored = 4usize;   // rounds that ended with every bit of the word restored
const kCount = 5usize;      // rounds where the multi-bit undo count rose by exactly one
const kReused = 6usize;     // rounds where the retired page came back as the 512 class's
const kListed = 7usize;     // whole-word rounds whose page ended LISTED
const kControl = 8usize;    // control rounds that took 8 cells of one page with no undo
// (row 532) the single-cell rounds' own counts
const kSTake = 9usize;      // the taker's swap took the one free bit, and the word read 0 after it
const kSUndo = 10usize;     // the undo's fetch_or gave the bit back
const kSRestored = 11usize; // the round ended with the word's bit restored
const kSCount = 12usize;    // Rule G's undo count rose by exactly one, the multi-bit count not at all
const kSReused = 13usize;   // the retired page came back as the same class with a new generation
const kSListed = 14usize;   // the page ended LISTED
const kSFresh = 15usize;    // the taker's cell is a 1024 cell other than the one it gave back

fn bump(k: usize, i: usize) { *word(k, i) = *word(k, i) + 1usize; }

fn controlRound(c: usize, k: usize, coll: Collect, tot: Total) {
  cleanup(coll);
  resetParks(c);
  let u0 = tot(10i32);
  if !fill8(c) { bump(k, kErr); return; }
  let e = checkFree8(c);
  if e == 0usize && tot(10i32) == u0 { bump(k, kControl); } else { *word(k, kErr) = *word(k, kErr) + e; }
}

// one stale round; whole: the filler takes a whole word (8 of 8 free) and the page is detached under it
// same (whole only): the page comes back as the SAME class (1024) with a new generation, not as the 512 class (row 701; a2)
fn staleRound(c: usize, k: usize, cells: usize, coll: Collect, tot: Total, pk: Peek, round: usize, whole: bool, same: bool) {
  cleanup(coll);
  resetParks(c);
  let nsz = if same { 1024usize } else { 512usize };
  // the 1024 page, as the filler will load its word: wholly free (partial) or with its 8 highest cells free (whole word)
  let keep = if whole { 56usize } else { 1usize };
  var n = 0usize;
  while n < keep { *word(cells, n) = libc.malloc(1024usize) as usize; n = n + 1usize; }
  let x0 = *word(cells, 0usize);
  if !whole { libc.free(x0 as *u8); }
  let expectOld = if whole { 0xFF00000000000000u64 } else { ones };
  let g1 = pk(x0, 64i32);
  st(c, cArmPre, 1usize);
  st(c, cDone, 0usize);
  st(c, cCmd, 1usize);
  if !waitFor(c, cParkedPre, 1usize) { bump(k, kErr); st(c, cRelPre, 1usize); waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize); return; }
  if u64.from(ld(c, cSeenOld)) != expectOld { bump(k, kErr); }
  // the page goes round: wholly free, retired, back from the pool as the 512 class's
  if whole { n = 0usize; while n < keep { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; } }
  cleanup(coll);
  // partial: cell 64 (in word 1) stays held, so the page cannot retire under the checks (the give-back timer retires a
  // wholly free page at any moment under giveback=now, and may decommit it); whole word: 120 cells stay held
  let nb = if same { 64usize } else if whole { 128usize } else { 65usize };
  n = 0usize;
  var onPage = 0usize;
  while n < nb {
    let b = libc.malloc(nsz) as usize;
    *word(cells, n) = b;
    stamp(b, nsz,7000000usize + round * 1000usize + n);
    if b >> 16usize == x0 >> 16usize { onPage = onPage + 1usize; }
    n = n + 1usize;
  }
  if onPage == nb && pk(x0, 64i32) != g1 { bump(k, kReused); }
  // the word as the filler loaded it: all 64 cells of word 0 free (partial), or its 8 highest (whole word)
  n = 0usize;
  if whole { n = 56usize; }
  while n < 64usize { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; }
  if pk(x0, 0i32) != expectOld { bump(k, kErr); }
  let u0 = tot(10i32);
  st(c, cArmTake, 1usize);
  st(c, cArmOr, 1usize);
  release(c, cRelPre);
  if !waitFor(c, cParkedTake, 1usize) {
    bump(k, kErr);                                  // the swap failed or no g2 test followed it
  } else {
    let want = if whole { expectOld } else { 0xFFu64 };
    if u64.from(ld(c, cSeenWant)) == want && pk(x0, 0i32) == (expectOld & (want ^ ones)) { bump(k, kTake); }
    var extra = 0usize;
    if whole {
      // another thread's allocation finds the page full and detaches it: the page is UNLISTED under the parked filler
      extra = libc.malloc(nsz) as usize;
      stamp(extra, nsz, 1usize);
      if pk(x0, 65i32) != 3u64 { bump(k, kErr); }
    }
    release(c, cRelTake);
    if waitFor(c, cParkedOr, 1usize) {
      if pk(x0, 0i32) == expectOld { bump(k, kUndo); }
      release(c, cRelOr);
    } else {
      bump(k, kErr);
    }
    if !waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize) { bump(k, kErr); }
    if pk(x0, 0i32) == expectOld { bump(k, kRestored); }
    if whole && pk(x0, 65i32) == 2u64 { bump(k, kListed); }
    if tot(10i32) == u0 + 1i64 { bump(k, kCount); }
    if extra != 0usize { libc.free(extra as *u8); }
  }
  release(c, cRelTake); release(c, cRelOr);
  waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize);
  // MB-W: every stamp of the new life is intact (free cells and held ones alike)
  n = 0usize;
  while n < nb {
    if !stampOk(*word(cells, n), nsz, 7000000usize + round * 1000usize + n) { bump(k, kStamp); }
    n = n + 1usize;
  }
  if whole {
    n = 0usize;
    while n < 56usize { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; }
  }
  n = 64usize;
  while n < nb { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; }
  *word(k, kErr) = *word(k, kErr) + checkFree8(c);
}

// (row 532) one single-cell round on lf_alloc: t is the taker's control block (a non-worker); the page comes back as the
// same 1024 class with a new generation
fn singleRound(t: usize, k: usize, cells: usize, coll: Collect, tot: Total, pk: Peek, round: usize) {
  cleanup(coll);
  resetParks(t);
  // the 1024 page, as the taker will load its word: cells 0 to 62 held, so only its highest cell (bit 63) is free
  var n = 0usize;
  while n < 63usize { *word(cells, n) = libc.malloc(1024usize) as usize; n = n + 1usize; }
  let x0 = *word(cells, 0usize);
  let expectOld = 0x8000000000000000u64;
  let g1 = pk(x0, 64i32);
  st(t, cN, 1usize);
  st(t, cOut, 0usize);
  st(t, cArmPre, 1usize);
  st(t, cDone, 0usize);
  st(t, cCmd, 1usize);
  if !waitFor(t, cParkedPre, 1usize) { bump(k, kErr); st(t, cRelPre, 1usize); waitFor(t, cDone, 1usize); return; }
  if u64.from(ld(t, cSeenOld)) != expectOld { bump(k, kErr); }
  // the page goes round: wholly free, retired, back from the pool as the same class's with a new generation; all 64 cells
  // taken (in bit order) and stamped, then the highest freed, so the word reads as the taker loaded it
  n = 0usize;
  while n < 63usize { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; }
  cleanup(coll);
  n = 0usize;
  var onPage = 0usize;
  while n < 64usize {
    let b = libc.malloc(1024usize) as usize;
    *word(cells, n) = b;
    stamp(b, 1024usize, 8000000usize + round * 1000usize + n);
    if b >> 16usize == x0 >> 16usize { onPage = onPage + 1usize; }
    n = n + 1usize;
  }
  if onPage == 64usize && pk(x0, 64i32) != g1 && (pk(x0, 64i32) & 0xFFu64) == (g1 & 0xFFu64) { bump(k, kSReused); }
  let given = *word(cells, 63usize);
  libc.free(given as *u8);
  if pk(x0, 0i32) != expectOld { bump(k, kErr); }
  let u9 = tot(9i32);
  let u10 = tot(10i32);
  st(t, cArmTake, 1usize);
  st(t, cArmOr, 1usize);
  release(t, cRelPre);
  if !waitFor(t, cParkedTake, 1usize) {
    bump(k, kErr);                                  // the swap failed or no park point followed it
  } else {
    if u64.from(ld(t, cSeenWant)) == expectOld && pk(x0, 0i32) == 0u64 { bump(k, kSTake); }
    // another thread's allocation finds the page full and detaches it: the page is UNLISTED under the parked taker
    let extra = libc.malloc(1024usize) as usize;
    if pk(x0, 65i32) != 3u64 { bump(k, kErr); }
    release(t, cRelTake);
    // the undo's park point, or the taker done without it: a taker parked there cannot finish, so whichever comes first
    // decides (a2s: the taker kept the cell and finished, with no undo)
    waitEither(t, cParkedOr, cDone);
    if ld(t, cParkedOr) == 1usize {
      if pk(x0, 0i32) == expectOld { bump(k, kSUndo); }
      release(t, cRelOr);
    } else {
      bump(k, kErr);
    }
    if !waitFor(t, cDone, 1usize) { bump(k, kErr); }
    if pk(x0, 0i32) == expectOld { bump(k, kSRestored); }
    if pk(x0, 65i32) == 2u64 { bump(k, kSListed); }
    if tot(9i32) == u9 + 1i64 && tot(10i32) == u10 { bump(k, kSCount); }
    libc.free(extra as *u8);
  }
  release(t, cRelTake); release(t, cRelOr);
  waitFor(t, cDone, 1usize);
  // every stamp of the new life is intact (the free cell and the held ones alike)
  n = 0usize;
  while n < 64usize {
    if !stampOk(*word(cells, n), 1024usize, 8000000usize + round * 1000usize + n) { bump(k, kStamp); }
    n = n + 1usize;
  }
  n = 0usize;
  while n < 63usize { libc.free(*word(cells, n) as *u8); n = n + 1usize; }
  // the taker's cell, taken after the undo: a 1024 cell, not the one it gave back; then freed by the main thread
  let p = ld(t, cOut);
  if p != 0usize && p != given && msize(p as *u8) == 1024usize { bump(k, kSFresh); }
  if p != 0usize { libc.free(p as *u8); }
}

fn envNum(name: cstr, dflt: usize) usize {
  let p = libc.getenv(name);
  if p as usize == 0usize { return dflt; }
  var v = 0usize;
  var i = 0usize;
  while true {
    let c = usize.from(*at(p, i));
    if c < 48usize || c > 57usize { break; }
    v = v * 10usize + (c - 48usize);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  if i == 0usize { dflt } else { v }
}

fn putStr(buf: *u8, pos: usize, s: cstr) usize {
  let n = strlen(s);
  copyLit(at(buf, pos), s, n);
  pos + n
}

fn putNum(buf: *u8, pos: usize, v: usize) usize {
  var digits = 1usize;
  var t = v;
  while t >= 10usize { t = t / 10usize; digits = digits + 1usize; }
  var x = v;
  var i = digits;
  while i > 0usize { i = i - 1usize; *at(buf, pos + i) = u8.from(48usize + x % 10usize); x = x / 10usize; }
  pos + digits
}

fn errLine(label: cstr, a: usize, mid: cstr, b: usize, tail: cstr, c: usize) {
  let buf = libc.malloc(256usize);
  var n = 0usize;
  n = putStr(buf, n, label); n = putNum(buf, n, a);
  n = putStr(buf, n, mid); n = putNum(buf, n, b);
  n = putStr(buf, n, tail); n = putNum(buf, n, c);
  *at(buf, n) = 10u8;
  var w = 0u32;
  WriteFile(GetStdHandle(0xFFFFFFF4u32), buf, u32.from(n + 1usize), &mut w, 0usize);
  // CNTEST_LOG=<file>: the same line appended there, since congo shows a passing test's stderr to nobody
  let lf = libc.getenv("CNTEST_LOG");
  if lf as usize != 0usize {
    let fh = CreateFileA(lf, 4u32, 3u32, 0usize, 4u32, 128u32, 0usize);
    if fh != 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFusize { WriteFile(fh, buf, u32.from(n + 1usize), &mut w, 0usize); CloseHandle(fh); }
  }
  libc.free(buf);
}

fn skipped() {
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every stale swap took its bits in one compare-and-swap");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every undo gave every taken bit back in one fetch_or");
  expectUInt(0u64, 0, "lfmulti: no stamp of the page's new life was overwritten");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every round ended with the word's bits restored");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: the multi-bit undo count rose by one each round");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: the retired page came back as the other class's page every round");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every whole-word round ended with the page listed");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: the control rounds took their cells normally");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every single-cell stale swap took its one bit");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every single-cell undo gave its bit back in its fetch_or");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every single-cell round ended with the bit restored");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: Rule G's undo count rose by one each single-cell round, the multi-bit count not at all");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: the retired page came back as the same class with a new generation every single-cell round");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: every single-cell round ended with the page listed");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: the taker's cell after each undo was a fresh 1024 cell");
  expect(true, "lfmulti: allocations equal frees at the end");
  expectUInt(0u64, 0, "lfmulti: no wrong cell, no stuck thread");
}

fn main() i32 {
  let m = GetModuleHandleA(null);
  let setHooks = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_lfSetHooks" as *u8);
  let setMulti = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_lfSetMultiHooks" as *u8);
  let collect = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_collect" as *u8);
  let design = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_design" as *u8);
  let total = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_lfTotal" as *u8);
  let peek = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_lfPeek" as *u8);
  let begin = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_workerBegin" as *u8);
  let end = GetProcAddress(m, &"cnmalloc_workerEnd" as *u8);
  if setHooks == 0usize || setMulti == 0usize || collect == 0usize || design == 0usize || total == 0usize || peek == 0usize || begin == 0usize { skipped(); return done(); }
  if (design as *u8 as DesignFn)() != 2i32 { skipped(); return done(); }
  let rounds = envNum("CNMULTI_ROUNDS", 20usize);
  let wholes = envNum("CNMULTI_WHOLE", 10usize);
  let sames = envNum("CNMULTI_SAME", 10usize);
  let singles = envNum("CNMULTI_SINGLE", 10usize);
  let coll = collect as *u8 as Collect;
  let tot = total as *u8 as Total;
  let pk = peek as *u8 as Peek;
  let c = libc.calloc(cWords, 8usize) as usize;
  let t = libc.calloc(cWords, 8usize) as usize;    // the taker's control block (row 532); cBegin and cEnd stay 0
  let k = libc.calloc(16usize, 8usize) as usize;
  let cells = libc.calloc(130usize, 8usize) as usize;
  st(c, cBegin, begin);
  st(c, cEnd, end);
  (setHooks as *u8 as SetHooks)(&hookPre as *u8 as usize, 0usize, 0usize, 0usize, &hookOr as *u8 as usize, 0usize);
  (setMulti as *u8 as SetMulti)(&hookTake as *u8 as usize, 0usize);
  let live0 = tot(0i32) - tot(1i32);         // cells live before the filler starts (the control block, the counts, cells)
  let wd = thread.start[usize, u64](c, &watchdog);
  let ft = thread.start[usize, u64](c, &filler);
  let tt = thread.start[usize, u64](t, &filler);
  // warm up: 14 cells, so the filler's fills grow 2, 4, 8 and its cache is empty again; each round's 8 cells are then
  // exactly one fill of 8, whose first allocation is the miss
  st(c, cN, 14usize);
  st(c, cDone, 0usize);
  st(c, cCmd, 1usize);
  waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize);
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < 14usize { libc.free(ld(c, cOut + i) as *u8); i = i + 1usize; }
  st(c, cN, 8usize);
  var r = 0usize;
  while r < 3usize { controlRound(c, k, coll, tot); r = r + 1usize; }
  r = 0usize;
  while r < rounds { staleRound(c, k, cells, coll, tot, pk, r, false, false); r = r + 1usize; }
  r = 0usize;
  while r < wholes { staleRound(c, k, cells, coll, tot, pk, rounds + r, true, false); r = r + 1usize; }
  r = 0usize;
  while r < sames { staleRound(c, k, cells, coll, tot, pk, rounds + wholes + r, true, true); r = r + 1usize; }
  r = 0usize;
  while r < singles { singleRound(t, k, cells, coll, tot, pk, rounds + wholes + sames + r); r = r + 1usize; }
  st(t, cDone, 0usize);
  st(t, cCmd, 2usize);
  waitFor(t, cDone, 1usize);
  tt.join();
  st(c, cDone, 0usize);
  st(c, cCmd, 2usize);
  waitFor(c, cDone, 1usize);
  ft.join();
  st(c, cStop, 1usize);
  wd.join();
  (setHooks as *u8 as SetHooks)(0usize, 0usize, 0usize, 0usize, 0usize, 0usize);
  (setMulti as *u8 as SetMulti)(0usize, 0usize);
  libc.free(cells as *u8);
  libc.free(t as *u8);
  cleanup(coll);
  let allocs = tot(0i32);
  let frees = tot(1i32);
  let all = rounds + wholes + sames;
  errLine("lfmulti: rounds ", rounds, " whole-word rounds ", wholes + sames," multi-bit undos ", usize.from(tot(10i32)));
  errLine("lfmulti: one-swap takes ", *word(k, kTake), " one-fetch_or undos ", *word(k, kUndo), " stamps hit ", *word(k, kStamp));
  errLine("lfmulti: restored ", *word(k, kRestored), " listed ", *word(k, kListed), " reused ", *word(k, kReused));
  errLine("lfmulti: single-cell rounds ", singles, " takes ", *word(k, kSTake), " undos ", *word(k, kSUndo));
  errLine("lfmulti: single-cell restored ", *word(k, kSRestored), " counted ", *word(k, kSCount), " reused ", *word(k, kSReused));
  errLine("lfmulti: single-cell listed ", *word(k, kSListed), " fresh ", *word(k, kSFresh), " Rule G undos ", usize.from(tot(9i32)));
  errLine("lfmulti: allocs ", usize.from(allocs), " frees ", usize.from(frees), " errors ", *word(k, kErr));
  expect(*word(k, kTake) == all, "lfmulti: every stale swap took its bits in one compare-and-swap");
  expect(*word(k, kUndo) == all, "lfmulti: every undo gave every taken bit back in one fetch_or");
  expectUInt(u64.from(*word(k, kStamp)), 0, "lfmulti: no stamp of the page's new life was overwritten");
  expect(*word(k, kRestored) == all, "lfmulti: every round ended with the word's bits restored");
  expect(*word(k, kCount) == all, "lfmulti: the multi-bit undo count rose by one each round");
  expect(*word(k, kReused) == all, "lfmulti: the retired page came back as the other class's page every round");
  expect(*word(k, kListed) == wholes + sames, "lfmulti: every whole-word round ended with the page listed");
  expect(*word(k, kControl) == 3usize, "lfmulti: the control rounds took their cells normally");
  expect(*word(k, kSTake) == singles, "lfmulti: every single-cell stale swap took its one bit");
  expect(*word(k, kSUndo) == singles, "lfmulti: every single-cell undo gave its bit back in its fetch_or");
  expect(*word(k, kSRestored) == singles, "lfmulti: every single-cell round ended with the bit restored");
  expect(*word(k, kSCount) == singles, "lfmulti: Rule G's undo count rose by one each single-cell round, the multi-bit count not at all");
  expect(*word(k, kSReused) == singles, "lfmulti: the retired page came back as the same class with a new generation every single-cell round");
  expect(*word(k, kSListed) == singles, "lfmulti: every single-cell round ended with the page listed");
  expect(*word(k, kSFresh) == singles, "lfmulti: the taker's cell after each undo was a fresh 1024 cell");
  expect(allocs - frees == live0 - 2i64, "lfmulti: allocations equal frees at the end");   // cells and t were live at live0
  expectUInt(u64.from(*word(k, kErr)), 0, "lfmulti: no wrong cell, no stuck thread");
  done()
}
